    "body": "\r\n## 🚀 Feature Proposal\r\n\r\nIn https://github.com/fastify/fastify/blob/d06287a9a612d218d26e3a94b248b5035d5c44cb/lib/request.js#L27-L29 there are the `ip`, `ips` and `hostname` properties that are currently set to `null`. Those are 3 pointers of 64 bytes each that we are carrying around with no specific needs as most code does not need them.\r\n\r\nThose are defined and set in https://github.com/fastify/fastify/blob/bf18412f2ba838fc06e3162a13ebcf88b5a283be/lib/route.js#L304-L315.\r\n\r\nI recommend that we move those definitions to getters similar to https://github.com/fastify/fastify/blob/bf18412f2ba838fc06e3162a13ebcf88b5a283be/lib/request.js#L36-L58. In order to support the `trustProxy`, I recommend those definitions to be overridden with another `Object.defineProperty()`.\r\n\r\nNote that the logger use them: https://github.com/fastify/fastify/blob/bf18412f2ba838fc06e3162a13ebcf88b5a283be/lib/logger.js#L54-L55",
